          "name": "How long do hair extensions last, and how often do they need maintenance?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "The lifespan of hair extensions depends on the installation method and home care routine. K-Tip and Brazilian Knots generally last three to six months before reapplication. Tape-In and Beaded Weft extensions usually require maintenance every six to eight weeks, while Microlink extensions are typically refreshed every two to four months. Premium Slavic human hair is reusable, so clients generally pay only for maintenance services and any additional hair needed."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "Will hair extensions damage my natural hair?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "When professionally installed, maintained, and matched to your hair type, hair extensions should not damage natural hair. During a consultation, your stylist evaluates your hair's density and condition before recommending the most suitable method. Techniques such as Microlink and Beaded Weft extensions are especially gentle because they require no heat or adhesive. Proper aftercare also plays an important role in maintaining healthy hair."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "Can I colour, heat-style, and wash my extensions like normal hair?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Yes. Because Luxe Aura Hair uses 100% human Slavic hair, the extensions can be washed, blow-dried, curled, and straightened similarly to natural hair. Sulphate-free shampoos and moisturizing conditioners are recommended to preserve the hair's quality. For the best colour match and to protect the extensions, professional salon colouring is recommended instead of at-home colouring."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "I have very short or very thin hair. Am I still a candidate for hair extensions?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Yes. Clients with short, fine, or thinning hair can often wear hair extensions when the appropriate method is selected. K-Tip and Brazilian Knots are commonly recommended for shorter hair, while lightweight Microlink extensions are often suitable for finer hair. During a consultation, the stylist will assess your hair's length, density, and condition to recommend the safest and most natural-looking option."
          }
        },
